    "title": "New Jersey Man Sentenced to 63 Months for Defrauding Elderly Victims of $1,130,406",
    "summary": "Federal prosecutors have secured a 63-month prison sentence against a New Jersey man who stole more than $1 million from elderly victims by falsely promising to invest their money. Antonio Petrosino, 61, of Union City, New Jersey, received the term on November 5th, 2026, from U.S. District Judge Stanley R. Chesler after pleading guilty to […]\nThe post New Jersey Man Sentenced to 63 Months for Defrauding Elderly Victims of $1,130,406 appeared first on The Daily Hodl.",
